+## 3. What this means for "how events get into Mixpanel and AWS"
+
+1. **AWS ingestion is real and now located**: API Gateway in **eu-central-1**
+   (two endpoints: custom-domain `d-gnyi890n7g` behind `t.imai.co`, and raw
+   `47dwgl20q6` used by the white-label pixel). It collects page-visit beacons
+   with full query strings (UTM/gclid) and fires at high-signal funnel moments
+   (trial activation, search page). The compute behind it (Lambda presumed) and
+   its write target (logs DB presumed) need AWS-console confirmation.
+2. **Server-side product/lifecycle events** do not go to AWS from the code we
+   can see — they go to an env-configured webhook (`CLOSE_WEBHOOK_URL`). The
+   receiver is the single most important remaining unknown: it decides whether
+   Mixpanel/Klaviyo/Close fan-out happens in AWS, make.com, or elsewhere.
+3. **Mixpanel is written only by the external pipeline** — nothing in any of
+   the five services in this repo talks to Mixpanel. Documentation of "events
+   → Mixpanel" is therefore blocked on pipeline access, not more code reading.
+4. **The platform itself is GCP end-to-end** (GCE + Cloud Run + GCS). AWS is
+   used only for the pixel collector (+ the S3 script bucket, ap-northeast-1).
+
+## 4. Answered vs. open (from plan §1.8)
+
+| # | Unknown (plan) | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1a | What receives CLOSE_WEBHOOK_URL | **OPEN** — env value needed (prod .env on discovery-prod, all `CLOSE_WEBHOOK_URL_<LABEL>` variants) |
+| 1b | What writes imai_events | **PARTIAL** — AWS API Gateway collector confirmed for page-visit data; webhook receiver for named events still unconfirmed |
+| 1c | Mixpanel sync job + user.mixpanel_sync writer | **OPEN** — not in repo; not GitHub-discoverable with current access |
+| 1d | t.imai.co hosting | **ANSWERED** — AWS API Gateway custom domain, eu-central-1 |
+| 1e | Which parts run on AWS | **ANSWERED** — pixel collector (API GW eu-central-1) + S3 script bucket (ap-northeast-1); everything else GCP/Cloudflare-Bubble |
+| 2 | Orphan events (high_value_signup, scheduled_demo_*, scheduled_ai_agent_call*) | **OPEN** — IMAI Close org / make.com / Calendly not accessible from this session (connector reaches a different Close org) |
+| 5 | Klaviyo sync mechanism | **OPEN** — needs Klaviyo admin or pipeline access |
+
+## 5. Access requests to close the remaining unknowns
+
+Concrete asks, in priority order:
+
+1. **`CLOSE_WEBHOOK_URL` (+ every `CLOSE_WEBHOOK_URL_<LABEL>`, `CANCELLATION_WEBHOOK_URL`)
+   values** from `backend/main/.env`, proxy env, and social-listening env on
+   `discovery-prod` (GCE, project "Leaders Prod"). One `grep -h WEBHOOK .env`
+   by anyone with SSH answers unknown 1a immediately.
+2. **AWS console access** (or an admin's 30-minute screen-share) for the account
+   owning eu-central-1 API Gateways `d-gnyi890n7g` + `47dwgl20q6`: list the
+   Lambda(s) behind them, their code/repo origin, and their DB/queue targets;
+   also S3 bucket `influencerprofiles` (ap-northeast-1) ownership. Likely also
+   hosts the logs DB (RDS?) and the Mixpanel sync — unknowns 1b/1c.
+3. **Logs-DB credentials** (read-only) — validates what the collector writes
+   (does imai_events itself receive pixel visits, or a sibling table?).
+4. **Mixpanel project admin** — Lexicon + ingestion logs (unknown 1c, Sprint 4 prep).
+5. **IMAI's Close org access** (current connector reaches the NewVoices org) +
+   **make.com** account — automations that likely emit the orphan events
+   (unknown 2) and possibly host the whole webhook fan-out.
+6. **GitHub org owner check**: are there IMAI repos this integration can't see
+   (lambda/pixel/sync code)? If the pipeline code is in GitHub, granting the
+   integration read access beats console spelunking.
+
